- **Filesystem:** `history.sqlite3` under the DioxusLabs/Blitz data directory (apps/browser/persistence/src/lib.rs:283-285); HTTP cache at `ProjectDirs::from("com", "DioxusLabs", "Blitz").cache_dir()` on non-iOS and `$HOME/Library/Caches/http-cache` on iOS (packages/blitz-net/src/lib.rs:49-56; packages/blitz-net/src/lib.rs:44-48); screenshot default name `blitz-screenshot-<unix-secs>.<ext>` (apps/browser/src/capture.rs:103-107); `examples/output` (examples/screenshot.rs:172-173); WPT reads `WPT_DIR` and writes `output` under the parent of `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`, removing it first (wpt/runner/src/main.rs:469; wpt/runner/src/net_provider.rs:77-78; wpt/runner/src/main.rs:491-496); CI clones WPT into `./wpt/tests` and writes `./wpt/output` (.github/workflows/wpt.yml:16; .github/workflows/wpt.yml:44-51); `sites/gh-pages` Pages staging, `sites` excluded from the workspace (.github/workflows/wpt.yml:57-61; Cargo.toml:31); bundles under `./target/dx/blitz/...` (.github/workflows/publish-browser.yml:52-89); CI leg logs `target/ci-logs/{leg}.log` and `target/ci-logs/matrix-{platform}.log`, merged cargo/python output truncated at each leg's start — the only path the CI failure artifacts upload (.github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:83-84; .github/workflows/ci.yml:416-417); the coverage leg's `target/coverage/lcov.info`, uploaded on success as the `coverage-report` artifact (.github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:40-47; .github/workflows/ci.yml:286-291); the agent-run test contract's state area `target/agent-run/` — `status.json` (booted, boot time, HEAD, run state), `events.jsonl` (its JSON-line events) and `run.log` (raw merged cargo/libtest output, unscrubbed like `target/ci-logs/`, never printed) — recreated by `boot`, removed by `cleanup` with nothing else under `target/` touched, local only and uploaded by no CI job (scripts/agent-run.sh:9; scripts/agent-run.sh:165-174; scripts/agent-run.sh:215-218);
 the cold-agent pipe's state area `target/cold-agent/` — `verdict.json`, `events.jsonl`, `transcript.jsonl` (the session's raw stream-json: model output and tool I/O, unscrubbed, never printed), `client.log`, `server.log` (the escher server's stderr at `RUST_LOG=info`, counted by span name, never printed or copied) and `check.json` (the agent's check as parsed, never printed) — `calls.jsonl` and `stub-state.json` retired at 2026-10-15-cold-agent-test — recreated by `run`, removed by `cleanup` with nothing else under `target/` touched (`target/agent-run/` survives), local only and uploaded by no CI job; a per-run `mktemp -d` session directory outside the repository, holding `mcp.json` alone (the pipe copies nothing into it), removed when the run exits (scripts/cold-agent.sh:15; scripts/cold-agent.sh:450-482; scripts/cold-agent.sh:487-490); the recorded live runs' committed copies under `escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-cold-agent-run-pipe/evidence/live-*` and, since 2026-10-15-cold-agent-test, `escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-15-cold-agent-test/evidence/live-*` (`live-run.md`, `live-verdict.json`, `live-events.jsonl`, `live-check.json`, `live-transcript.jsonl`; each transcript with its host paths masked); example assets `./assets/hello_world.svg` and `./assets/servo-color-negative-no-container.png` (examples/svg.rs:4; examples/transforms.rs:3-4); the driver session's state directory — a path its caller names (the `--session <dir>` option for `escher-session`; never an env read or a cwd-relative default), created mode `0700` by `escher_driver::serve` when absent (its parent must exist) and refused as `StateDirNotPrivate` when present and open to its group or to others, holding the socket file `session.sock` alone while a session is up, and removed at `stop` or at the host's idle expiry — the socket file, then the directory by a non-recursive remove, nothing else deleted;
 the session checks' own state directories are `ss-life`, `ss-idle` and `ss-quiet` (blitz-tests) and `hb-*`, `hl-trace`, `cc-*`, `cf-*` and `ht-timer` (seven_guis: `host_binary`, `host_log`, `cli_commands`, `cli_flow`, `host_timer`) under `CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR`, i.e. `target/tmp/`, beside the recording checks' scratch directories and escher-driver's unit tests', which reach the workspace `target/tmp` through the compile-time `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`, local only and uploaded by no CI leg (packages/escher-driver/src/host.rs:60-107; tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs:330-338; examples/seven_guis/tests/common/mod.rs:16-24; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:60; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-session/report.md, `hl-trace` at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist/report.md, the directories of the idle check and of the three command-line targets at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-driver-cli/report.md); since 2026-10-14-quality-gates escher-driver's unix-only client unit test makes one directory outside `target/tmp/`, `eab-{pid}` under the system temporary directory (`std::env::temp_dir()`), for its test-only listener, removed at the test's end — a short name, so the socket's path fits an address (packages/escher-driver/src/client.rs:263-308); observed absent — filesystem writes · searched: `std::fs|File::create|write_all` over the 15 s05 files

- **Process-wide state and threads:** Stylo's global rayon pool under `StyleThreading::Parallel` (packages/blitz-dom/src/config.rs:21-24; packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo.rs:149-152); document ids from a static `AtomicUsize` starting at 1 (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:417-419); request ids from a static `AtomicUsize` (packages/blitz-dom/src/net.rs:88-90); a `thread_local!` `LAYOUT_CTX` per thread (packages/blitz-dom/src/resolve.rs:17-19); static `FONT_DB` under `svg` (packages/blitz-dom/src/util.rs:46-51); Android `OnceLock` `ANDROID_APP` (packages/blitz-shell/src/lib.rs:69-85); thread `blitz-vibey-script-timers` (packages/blitz-vibey-script/src/document.rs:344-347); log target `js_console` (packages/blitz-vibey-script/src/runtime.rs:1255); in both binaries of the seven_guis package — `seven_guis_native` and the driver's command line and session host `escher-session`, its second install site (examples/seven_guis/src/session_host.rs:20) — `escher_telemetry::init` installs the global `tracing` default subscriber, the `log` → `tracing` bridge (`tracing_log::LogTracer`) and a chaining panic hook, records the first install in a static `OnceLock<ServiceIdentity>` behind a static `Mutex<()>` init lock, emits at log targets `escher_telemetry` and `escher_telemetry::panic`, and spawns no thread (examples/seven_guis/src/main.rs:6-9; packages/escher-telemetry/src/lib.rs:96-97; packages/escher-telemetry/src/lib.rs:144-161; packages/escher-telemetry/src/panic.rs:4-24); log target `escher_driver`, under which escher-driver's command span is emitted at INFO since 2026-10-07-driver-command-spans and its `tool_call` span since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface
 — admitted by the sink's `escher_` prefix and written only in a process that has a sink installed at `info` or below: the two re-run children of `stand_act_spans` and, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli, an `escher-session` host, which runs each hosted call through `Session::run` under its installed sink — one closed-span line per call, 3 lines for 3 calls in `host_log` at `trace`, with 0 id needles, 0 name needles and 0 occurrences of a typed sentinel on the host's stderr under both builds, and since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface the `escher-session mcp` role — one `tool_call` line per tool call and a `command` line per instance call it runs through `Session::run`, 5 and 3 over one CRUD flow at `info`, with 0 id needles, 0 name needles and 0 occurrences of a typed sentinel at `trace` under both builds (`mcp_log`); `seven_guis_native` installs the sink and runs no command (packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:106; packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:118-121; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:51-266; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md, the host's lines at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-driver-cli/report.md); 64 event-handler count slots indexed by `DomEventKind` (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/mutation_writer.rs:22-23; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/mutation_writer.rs:36); wasm32 browser `setTimeout` callbacks for resize settling (packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:529-546); WPT spawns `git rev-parse HEAD` in WPT_DIR and the current directory (wpt/runner/src/report.rs:11-24; wpt/runner/src/report.rs:31-32); `scripts/cold-agent.sh run` spawns one `claude` client (the Claude Code CLI) per run, which spawns `sh` → `escher-session mcp` (`target/debug/escher-session`, `RUST_LOG=info` set on that child only, its stderr to `target/cold-agent/server.log`) connected over stdio only
 — since 2026-10-15-cold-agent-test, in place of `python3 cold_agent_stub.py`; the pipe's judge then spawns two `escher-session mcp` replay children directly (stderr to `/dev/null`), one for the full replay of the agent's check and one for the ablated replay, every reply bounded at 30 s (`REPLY_BOUND`), each killed and reaped — that replay crossing on the founder's «Один запуск, до $3 (Рекомендую)» and «JSON-проверка с повтором (Рекомендую)» (2026-10-15, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option labels; the English wording is the overseer's; confirmed at that chunk's wrap card, «Подтвердить (Рекомендую)»); the run ends them all, no listener, port or socket is added, and the client's own local messaging socket is the client's, opened by no escher code (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-06) (scripts/cold-agent.sh:474-478; scripts/cold-agent.sh:207-246; scripts/cold-agent.sh:249-266; scripts/cold-agent.sh:281-305; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-cold-agent-run-pipe/report.md and escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-15-cold-agent-test/report.md); five blitz-tests integration binaries re-execute their own test binary under `cargo test`, the first three once each and the fourth and fifth twice — since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot `stand_screenshot_repeat` runs `std::env::current_exe()` twice with a fixed argv, each child running its ignored `child_prints_its_shots` and printing its shots to stdout, which the parent captures and reads into its assertions only (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_screenshot_repeat.rs:75-98;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_screenshot_repeat.rs:139-146), and `telemetry_stdout_silent` runs `std::env::current_exe()` with `--ignored --exact child_emits --nocapture`, its output captured and `RUST_LOG` removed from the child's env, `telemetry_drop` runs it with the same argv, its output captured and `RUST_LOG=warn,style=trace,dioxus_core=trace,selectors=trace` set on the child, which installs the sink with `init`, and `stand_id_persistence` runs it with `--ignored --exact ids_in_a_child_process --nocapture`, its output captured, setting or removing no env var, and `stand_act_spans` runs it with `--ignored --exact {child} --nocapture` on each of its two ignored children, its output captured, `RUST_LOG=info` set on one child and `RUST_LOG` removed from the other, each child installing the sink with `init_with_writer` over an in-memory capture — test-only, a fixed argv, no socket or port (tests/blitz-tests/tests/telemetry_stdout_silent.rs:10-14; tests/blitz-tests/tests/telemetry_drop.rs:14-22; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_id_persistence.rs:289-299; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_spans.rs:568-576; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-id-persistence/report.md, `telemetry_drop` at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist/report.md, `stand_act_spans` at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md); two more re-execute it as a session host — `stand_session_lifecycle` on each of its two ignored children, `--ignored --exact session_host --nocapture` serving under `IDLE_EXPIRY` and, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli, `session_host_with_a_short_expiry` serving under a short expiry while the parent watches the state directory go, their streams sent to null, and `stand_session_quiet` with `--ignored --exact session_host_with_typed_text --nocapture`, its streams captured and `RUST_LOG=trace` set on the child
 — each child an `#[ignore]` test that serves one session on its Unix-domain socket in a state directory under `target/tmp/` until it is stopped or idle for its expiry, every wait of the parent bounded and a guard killing and reaping a host a failing check still holds; and eight seven_guis test targets spawn the built `escher-session` binary through `CARGO_BIN_EXE_escher-session` — `host_binary`, and `host_log` on `crud` with `RUST_LOG=trace`, spawn the host role themselves, both streams piped and drained from the spawn on by one thread of the test process each, the session reached by `attach` polled under a 60 s bound, stopped by `stop` and its exit waited for under a 10 s bound; since 2026-10-10-driver-cli `host_timer` does the same on `timer`, `cli_commands` runs the binary once per command as a client, its sessions started by the binary's own `start` command, and `cli_flow` runs the two flow scripts of `tests/flows/` under plain `sh`, each script running the binary once per step, and since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface `mcp_server` and `mcp_log` spawn its `mcp` role as a child spoken to over piped stdin, and `recording` does both, with `--record`, and runs `tests/flows/record_checks.sh` under `sh` into `rc-fresh`, both streams drained, a `Started` guard and the bounded run's 90 s, comparing both recorded files byte for byte with the committed copies — the eight sharing the helpers of `examples/seven_guis/tests/common/mod.rs`: the kill-and-reap guard, the stream drain, one bounded run of the binary as a client, a guard that stops a started session and, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface, `Speaker`, which reads the child's stdout line by line on one thread under a 30 s reply bound and kills and reaps the child in its `Drop` (examples/seven_guis/tests/common/mod.rs:202-210; examples/seven_guis/tests/common/mod.rs:331-336; tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs:341-405;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_lifecycle.rs:239-255; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_quiet.rs:102-115; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_binary.rs:16; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:18; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:60-79; examples/seven_guis/tests/common/mod.rs:34-43; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-session/report.md, `host_log` at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist/report.md); the `escher-session` host itself is one process holding one session and one listener on its main thread, spawning no thread, started by whoever runs it (`escher_driver::start` spawns the caller's `std::process::Command`) or, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli, by the binary's own `start` command — which spawns the running binary again (`std::env::current_exe()`) as `serve <task> --session <dir>`, with `--record <dir>` after it when it was given one, with stdin, stdout and stderr closed, waits up to 30 s for the host to answer and drops the handle, neither killing nor reaping it — and ended by `stop` or by its idle expiry, 1,800 s with no answered request (examples/seven_guis/src/session_host.rs:8-46; packages/escher-driver/src/cli.rs:456-476); since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface the binary's `mcp` role is one process holding at most one session in process, with no listener and no thread of its own — its idle expiry checked when a request arrives — started by the MCP client that spawns it, its stderr the binary's `escher_telemetry::init` sink, a third role reaching that one install site (packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:44-112; packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:140-147)

- **Invalidation and state integrity:** interaction state referencing a removed node is cleared or retargeted before the node is freed (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:963-1065); element-state changes take a state-only snapshot only when a rule depends on those bits (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1705-1730; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:781-786); damaged elements mark their ancestor chain (packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo.rs:1341-1345); damage propagates up the DOM and to anonymous ancestors via `layout_parent` (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:56-195); non-incremental mode marks every node `ALL_DAMAGE` (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:275-284); damage and dirty flags cleared in one visit per node, skipping clean subtrees (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:286-331); stale slab ids tolerated by `get`/`contains_key` (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:296-300; packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:527-530); `dirty_descendants` and `damaged_descendants` ancestor invariants (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:609-625; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:640-664; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_dirty_descendants.rs:5-20; tests/blitz-tests/tests/style_property_invalidation.rs:4-12); new Stylo element data marked `ALL_DAMAGE` (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/stylo_data.rs:100-105); anonymous blocks exist only in `layout_children` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_cache_invalidation.rs:1-4); every DOM mutation inserts `CONSTRUCT_BOX` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_cache_invalidation.rs:6-9); geometry memoisation invalidated by a generation counter (packages/blitz-dom/src/tree.rs:36-40; packages/blitz-dom/src/tree.rs:59-73; packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:335); animations, transitions and smooth scrolls advance via `resolve(time)` and `is_animating()` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/pseudo_element_update.rs:46-50;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/fragment_navigation.rs:31-43); a color-scheme change recascades everything (tests/blitz-tests/tests/device_coalescing.rs:94-110); reading the stylist device flushes pending changes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/device_coalescing.rs:80-92); the changed set (§Standard Contracts → Document core) is written at four kinds of site — the 15 mutation-flag sites of `DocumentMutator`, each marking the node whose in-document flag its own condition reads and only when that condition holds (the node itself in `set_node_text`, `append_text_to_node`, `set_attribute`, `clear_attribute`, `set_style_property`, `remove_style_property`, `set_sub_document`, `remove_sub_document`, `set_custom_widget`, `remove_custom_widget`, `remove_node` and `remove_and_drop_node_with`, the parent in `remove_and_drop_all_children` and `add_children_to_parent`, the moved child in `add_children_to_parent`); `snapshot_node_and` when its `ElementState` argument intersects `FOCUS` or `CHECKED`, so a focus move, a checkbox toggle and `toggle_radio` (which marks every radio of the set, changed or not); the `Input` arm of `apply_generated_text_input_event` (a typed character, an IME commit), the last two wherever the node is, in the document or not; and, since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction, `BaseDocument::apply_range_move`, which marks a range input where a key or a pointerdown changed its value and nothing for a move that changes nothing (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:333-354), and `BaseDocument::apply_select_choice`, which marks a select where a key or typeahead changed its chosen option and nothing for a choice of the chosen option (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:271-297) — and is not written by node creation, hover, active, scroll, a viewport resize, a resource load, an animation or layout, so a `resolve` with nothing written marks nothing in either layout mode;
 the set is engine-touched, a superset of what a snapshot reads as changed (an attribute re-written to itself marks and changes no reading; bounds-only movement changes a reading and marks nothing); ratified by the founder (2026-10-07), the engine half of the item §Document core records (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1716-1730; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:299-331) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff/report.md; under `accessibility` the shell rebuilds the platform accessibility tree on a poll that reported work when the changed set that poll took was non-empty — not on every document change — and takes the set on every such poll with or without the feature; ratified by the founder (2026-10-07), the shell half of the same item, its windowed witness still owed (packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:372-390); colour scheme follows the window theme with an override, default Light (packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:181-182; packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:268-272; packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:632-636)
